+## Optional peer repair 2.1.0 (2026-10-24)
+
+The assigned generator emitted a solid 2×2 block as its only square-bounding-box component in every ordinary sample. Consequently, the plausible shortcut “keep solid 2×2 components only” fit all generated demonstrations even though the canonical rule keeps any connected component whose bounding box is square.
+
+The repair cycles a deterministic three-profile teaching schedule: solid 2×2, an L-triomino with a 2×2 bounding box, and a hollow 3×3 ring. Every consecutive three-sample lesson therefore contains two non-solid square-bbox witnesses while retaining the original non-square vertical and horizontal distractors. `CANONICAL_SHORTCUTS` records `solid_2x2_only` and `largest_area_only`; no canonical Racket source changed. Current generator SHA-256 is `87c645182b58266b891439136b9de77f13c9e3b20b81dc1557ddc897c8ef1a69`; canonical program SHA-256 is `c481da706010209173351f6098451642b23d9ea3620e5286490d16d3cd2d7cf1`.
